STEP 6 PART 2 of 2 — THE COMPOSING INVOCATION (full source, per the rail that a deleted probe's output alone is a lead, not evidence) AND THE LANDED RECORD.

Written as `packages/benchmark/compose-activation-record.probe.mts`, run once with real node, then deleted from the tree (`git status --porcelain -- packages/benchmark` shows no residue). Recreate and re-run it verbatim:
```ts
import { writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { composeActivationRecord } from "./src/activation-record.js";
import { PINNED_SPEC_SHA256 } from "./src/claim-ladder-contract.js";

const familyEvidence = [
  { countLine: null, exitCode: 1, familyId: "repository" },
  { countLine: "Test Files  2 passed (2)", exitCode: 0, familyId: "property" },
  { countLine: null, exitCode: 1, familyId: "fault" },
  { countLine: null, exitCode: 1, familyId: "security" },
  { countLine: "Test Files  6 passed (6)", exitCode: 0, familyId: "migration" },
  { countLine: "Test Files  22 passed (22)", exitCode: 0, familyId: "integration" },
  { countLine: null, exitCode: 1, familyId: "e2e" },
  { countLine: null, exitCode: 1, familyId: "packaging" },
  { countLine: "Test Files  24 passed (24)", exitCode: 0, familyId: "benchmark" },
  { countLine: null, exitCode: null, familyId: "independent-review" },
];

const campaignVerdicts = {
  "G-J1": "UNKNOWN", "G-L1": "UNKNOWN", "G-L2": "UNKNOWN", "G-L3": "UNKNOWN",
  "G-L3-accept": "UNKNOWN", "G-L3-budget": "UNKNOWN", "G-L3-cost": "UNKNOWN",
  "G-L3-speed": "UNKNOWN", "G-L4": "UNKNOWN", "G-L4-userstudy": "UNKNOWN",
  "G-L5": "UNKNOWN", "G-UI": "UNKNOWN", "G-overhead": "UNKNOWN",
} as const;

const result = composeActivationRecord({
  binding: null,
  campaignVerdicts,
  claimSentences: [],
  familyEvidence,
  pinnedSpecSha256: PINNED_SPEC_SHA256,
  scopeNotEstablished: [
    "No GO_ACTIVATE binding exists: the board holds a standing authorization that names no quiesce, import, backup or distribution generation (comment-c34269c9).",
    "The live legacy quiesce (task-e60b874bac924a6b9c255cb8c924041f) was deferred by the human operator on 2026-08-27 until the PR #3 epic closes, so no quiesce generation has been produced.",
    "The cutover activation tooling is absent: successor rows task-b254847909ca4199a70a3a06173f1cd9 and task-c4321b6f0dbe439cb4948a3b27302d81 own the act and neither has landed.",
    "This record certifies NOT_ACTIVATED. It is a statement of evidence about one commit and grants no success verdict, no activation and no scoped claim.",
  ],
  sourceCommit: process.argv[2] ?? "",
});

if (!result.ok) {
  console.error(JSON.stringify(result));
  process.exit(1);
}
const output = { ...result.record, familyEvidence };
writeFileSync(process.argv[3] ?? "", JSON.stringify(output, null, 2) + "\n", "utf8");
console.log(JSON.stringify(result.record.activation));
console.log("reachedRung=" + result.record.reachedRung);
```
Invocation and stdout:
```
node packages/benchmark/compose-activation-record.probe.mts ee36952e2df74b0ebc23d166879088880547150f packages/benchmark/campaigns/task-09008b4cb39c4a15aa661540d20e9b9b/activation-record.json
{"refusal":{"code":"ACTIVATION_BINDING_ABSENT","layer":"GA_ACTIVATION_BINDING"},"status":"NOT_ACTIVATED"}
reachedRung=L0
PROBE_EXIT=0
```
`claimSentences` is deliberately `[]`: at L0 the pinned spec licenses NO sentence, so proposing one would only produce a CLAIM_REFUSED. The record says nothing rather than saying something refusable.

THE RECORD, 135 lines, 2-space JSON with LF, at `packages/benchmark/campaigns/task-09008b4cb39c4a15aa661540d20e9b9b/activation-record.json`: schemaVersion `moe-ga-activation-record/1`, activationRow this row, sourceCommit ee36952e…, reachedRung L0, claimSentences [], ten gateFamilies in roster order, four scopeNotEstablished sentences, and `activation: {"refusal":{"code":"ACTIVATION_BINDING_ABSENT","layer":"GA_ACTIVATION_BINDING"},"status":"NOT_ACTIVATED"}`. It also embeds `familyEvidence` so the checker can RE-RUN the resolver rather than trust the table.

THE INDEPENDENT CHECKER, `activation-record.test.ts` beside it: re-resolves the ten verdicts through `resolveAll` over the embedded evidence and compares to `gateFamilies`; re-resolves the rung through `resolveReachedRung` over the campaign's own verdicts and compares to `reachedRung`; re-derives `admitActivationBinding(null)` and compares to `activation.refusal`; asserts `claimSentences` is empty, the pinned digest matches `PINNED_SPEC_SHA256`, and `sourceCommit` is 40-hex AND `git merge-base --is-ancestor <commit> HEAD` exits 0 via execFileSync; and asserts the file TEXT contains neither `"ACTIVE"` nor `firstAuthoritativeCommand`, so a hand-edited extra key cannot slip past a typed read. Its first arm is an APPLICABILITY BOUND: it throws unless `activation.status` is one of the two the composer can emit, so a future record about a real activation cannot reuse this proof.

`(cd packages/benchmark && pnpm exec vitest run --root ../.. packages/benchmark/campaigns)` -> `Test Files  3 passed (3)` / `Tests  22 passed | 7 skipped (29)`.

TWO IMPORT NOTES. (1) The checker takes `GA_ACTIVATION_RECORD_SCHEMA_VERSION`, `GA_ACTIVATION_WORK_REF` and `admitActivationBinding` through the BARE `@moe/benchmark` specifier, which also proves this row's new barrel exports resolve for a consumer. (2) `resolveAll`, `resolveReachedRung` and `PINNED_SPEC_SHA256` are NOT on that root surface, so they are imported relatively from inside their own package. I did not publish them: widening a package's public API to satisfy a test is a scope expansion this row was not given.

MEASURED LIMITATION, disclosed rather than papered over: `packages/benchmark/tsconfig.json` includes only `src/**/*.ts`, and no other tsconfig covers `campaigns/**`, so campaign checkers — mine and both siblings — are TYPECHECKED BY NOTHING in the standing gates; vitest only transpiles them. I ran an ad-hoc `tsc --noEmit` over my checker with the repo's standard strict flag set: EXIT 0. That is a one-time measurement, not a gate, and the gap belongs to whoever owns the campaigns lane.
